@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Temporary Recommended Trades protections — build 2245
+
+## Confirmed gap and shared boundary
+
+Production v1.22.29/build2244, commit a17f9113868c3b9dcc3dd68d0b02613a2ad1de98, tree b6c1729a5559167557dcc7b4eaa677c81e00b588, was ready at the bounded baseline check. A real authenticated 320×432 disposable baseline replay confirmed that Recommended Trades had no pre-search protection picker. Shop and offer-adjustment controls already existed, and the native search already honored `protected_assets` using exact trade asset IDs. No new generator, qualification rule or protection formula is introduced.
+
+The existing recommendation pipeline filters protected IDs from the active franchise's discovery and construction pools before candidate evaluation. Every variant, qualified result and exploratory result comes from those filtered pools. Original-franchise pick identity is retained: an owned `2029-R1-1` is distinct from an acquired `2029-R1-3`. The source-compatible test population includes both, not interchangeable year/round placeholders.
+
+## State and presentation
+
+A Recommended Trades-only temporary list is kept in the existing authorized tab/workspace storage. It is distinct from legacy draft/Shop adjustment constraints. Generate sends this list through the existing exact constraint; Evaluate continues to use its own draft constraints. Opening, adding, removing or clearing protections makes no search/provider request and changes no saved preference. Existing saved Custom Protect flags continue to merge through the established personal constraint boundary; clearing temporary controls does not clear those flags.
+
+The manager can inspect owned assets, protect an exact one, remove it, or clear the list. Exact IDs and original-franchise metadata are shown with picks. Selection is rechecked against current prepared ownership on restoration and scoped to the authorized account, league and franchise. An asset no longer in the owned universe is not offered as a temporary owned protection. The server continues to enforce ordinary authorization, source compatibility, admission and final evaluation. Workspace storage is not an authorization mechanism.
+
+Each completed search stores the effective constraint returned by the native search, including existing saved Custom protections when applicable. The visible completed summary and separately retained earlier-search disclosure show that snapshot, never the newly edited controls. Legacy results without a retained constraint snapshot are explicitly unknown. A completed zero-qualified search remains distinct from deferral/failure; displaying restrictions makes no claim that they caused rejection. Existing search results, Evaluate assets/order/valuation/strategy, selected comparisons and contextual navigation retain their existing evidence qualifications.
+
+## Verification and limits
+
+Focused regression uses actual authenticated routes, native prepared Sleeper projection and Market fixtures, the canonical search/evaluator and normal memory admission inside a real 2 GiB disposable container. Controls exercise a protected player, own first versus acquired first, full outgoing-pool filtering, returned qualified/exploratory rows, keyboard/touch removal, clearing, original-results labeling, contextual Back to an evaluated draft, comparison preservation, reload, league switching and a real completed empty-candidate search. Four responsive sizes are 320×432, 375×667, 390×844 and desktop1280×900. Fixtures prove deterministic implementation behavior; they are not live owner offers, a production capacity assertion or physical iPhone/Safari acceptance.
+
+Initial focused failures are preserved externally. One asserted hidden prior-results text before opening its disclosure. Another compared the whole restored assessment, although the existing restore path truthfully adds retained-state metadata. The corrected assertions open the disclosure and independently compare the exact evaluation and ordered proposal. No application guard, calculation, source compatibility or browser assertion was removed to make these controls pass.
+
+No changes to canonical Market/Custom formulas, scoring, Sleeper projections/results, optimal lineups, submitted Sleeper lineups, exact picks, bilateral thresholds, source acquisition, FOIS grades, resource reservations or admission arithmetic. The cap stays 2 GiB, Trade256+128MiB and FOIS768MiB. Final exact-source focused, full canonical, hosted, resource, publication and production evidence is recorded in the immutable external handoff. Production search acceptance is separate and must stop on capacity deferral. No production search is required merely to publish this UI correction.
